.TH STIME 2
.SH NAME
stime \- set time
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B "stime(tp)"
.B "long *tp;"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B stime
sets the system's idea of the time and date.
Time, pointed to by
.IR tp ,
is measured in seconds from 00:00:00 GMT Jan 1, 1970.
Only the
super-user may use this call.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
date(1), time(2), ctime(3)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Zero is returned if the time was set; \-1 if user is not the super-user.
.SH ASSEMBLER
(stime = 25.)
.TP
PDP-11:
.nf
R0, R1 = time
sys stime
.fi
.TP
8086:
.nf
BX = 25
AX = time1
DX = time2
int 0Xf1
.fi
.sp
